From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: knapcio <knapcio@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 18 Oct 2026 22:39:18 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 23/30] S2: G6_CP_STEP_ROWS=n caps a step past R at n rows and
 sizes the CP fabric for n (default off)

Since #94 a split run past R shares batched steps, so the CP fabric and the CP graphs at every bucket past R are sized
for the widest S2 step: sessions x (mtp + 1) = 24 rows at 8 sessions / MTP 2, 1.358 GB pinned + registered per rank at
TP=4 (8 rows: 0.453 GB). With G6_CP_STEP_ROWS=n (at least the rows before #94, the boot names it; clamped to the widest
S2 step) the fabric is sized for n, and Driver::step forms rounds so that no step past R carries more than n rows:
while a session past R decodes and the decoding sessions' rows do not fit, a round takes at most n / (mtp + 1)
sessions, those past R first (request-id order), and the others sit it out the way a grow stall does (Batch::round
leaves their state untouched). Cycles: every decoding session gets one round per cycle; a round without a session past
R keeps the full batch. A session counts as past R when length + mtp > cp_after (an upper bound of its verify context;
cp_after = the largest bucket <= R, so ctx > cp_after exactly when the engine runs the CP block). capture_all skips the
main widths above n at buckets past R. G6_CP_STEP_SEG=1: a round past R takes only sessions past R, so a session below
R never runs the CP path (whose LSE merge rounds differently) because of a resident long session.

Every input is replicated state (the scheduler's decoding sessions, grow stalls, Batch lengths, boot constants); the
knob joins the scheduler digest, the bootstrap agreement and the S2 runtime signature only when set. m4sim applies the
same rounds to its --s2 loop. One stderr line per rank when rounds become capped or uncapped.

Host test s2/tests/cp_rows_test.cpp (scripts/host_tests.sh): cp_after against the bucket rule for every context, the
boot parse, hand-made cycles, and Driver::step over random requests (past R from the start, crossing R, insert rules,
grow stalls) at n = 8, 12 and SEG: every request emits its solo tokens, no step past R wider than n, SEG never mixes,
two ranks agree on every digest and step, waits bounded; unengaged knob = the knob-off step sequence.
