 | `G6_CP_R` | `SHARE_LIMIT` | the first R tokens of KV are replicated on every rank. Pages past R are spread across ranks. Under S2 it is also the largest request that shares decode steps. A multiple of 64; R is always a decode bucket boundary (a value off the 2048 doubling is added as a bucket of its own) |
 | `G6_CP_S3` | 1 | CP combine order (1 = head-group overlap order, same arithmetic as 0) |
 | `G6_CP_ONECHAIN` | 0 | 1 = past R, the other ranks' head groups run as one attention call of 48 heads instead of three of 16 (the scores, softmax, context and merge kernels once per layer, not three times; their partials are published after it, in the order `G6_CP_S3=0` uses). Byte-exact. TP=4 only, and not with `G6_ATTN_FLIP`; about 1.3 MB a row of the CP fabric's rows (`G6_CP_MMAX`) for the gathered queries and the call's scratch |
+| `G6_CP_STEP_ROWS` | 0 | S2 (`--serve`): a step past R carries at most this many rows, and the CP fabric is sized for it instead of the widest S2 step (`--s2-sessions` x (`--mtp` + 1) = 24 rows, 1.358 GB pinned per rank at TP=4; 8 rows = 0.453 GB). While a session past R decodes and the decoding sessions' rows do not fit, a round takes at most this many / (`--mtp` + 1) sessions, those past R first, and the others go in the next round (every decoding session gets one round per cycle); rounds without a session past R keep the full batch. At least the rows of a solo or prompt step past R (the boot names the minimum: 8 with DFlash2), larger values are clamped to the widest S2 step. 0 = off (every round takes every session). The cap changes only which sessions share a step, never a session's rows, positions or sampling: sessions past R give the same tokens as without it; a session below R that is left out of a past-R round runs that round on the replicated path instead of the CP path, whose LSE merge rounds differently (see `G6_CP_STEP_SEG`). Part of the bootstrap agreement when set |
+| `G6_CP_STEP_SEG` | 0 | with `G6_CP_STEP_ROWS`: 1 = a round past R takes only sessions past R, so a session below R never runs the CP path because a long session is resident (its output is the one it has without that session); a mix that would fit in one step takes two rounds. Part of the bootstrap agreement when set |
 | `G6_CP_PF_VERIFY` | 1 | check every KV page staged to another rank against a hash |
 | `G6_CP_PF_HASH2` | 1 | the fast HASH2 page hash for that check (build flag `-DG6_CP_PF_HASH2=1`). This is the "H2" in K1H2 |
 | `G6_PROGRESS_ISOLATE` | 1 | just before the first fabric barrier, move every thread that is not a fabric proxy thread off the proxy CPUs (the cores of the proxies this rank started, see `--proxy-cpu`) so no worker thread can preempt a progress thread. 0 = off (the A/B switch). Anything but 0/1 is rejected at startup. A thread that cannot be moved is named in the log |
